{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999628-pseudo-scientific-names-for-supernatural-creatures","id":999628,"title":"Pseudo-scientific names for supernatural creatures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T02:16:06-08:00","id":999628,"title":"Pseudo-scientific names for supernatural creatures","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm looking for some pseudo-scientific names that would be used describe or refer to supernatural creatures of World of Darkness.<br /> In my chronicle, the Technocraty have redacted many documents (mission report, lab experiment...) in which they refer to supernatural creatures.<br /> Being the Technocraty, scientific and all, they obviously can't use simple words like Vampire or Werewolf and needs to have their own scientific name for supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> Do you have any ideas for those &quot;scientific names&quot;?<br /> <br /> I've found an example that could be used to refer to vampire: Class-V Hematophagous","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:22:28-08:00","id":999630,"title":"","content":"could use DNA's term of GLS for Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:29:15-08:00","id":999632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999628-pseudo-scientific-names-for-supernatural-creatures?p=999630#post999630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could use DNA's term of GLS for Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, maybe... but, what's GLS ? Homo sapiens glutaminase (<i>GLS</i>) is the best result I've found with a google search.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:43:30-08:00","id":999684,"title":"","content":"The problem would be giving them some kind of taxonomic label that falls in line with existing taxonomy. I can see those being consistently rejected by Progenitors, for a variety of reasons. There's no real relation, they're just an error in reality, etc..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999628-pseudo-scientific-names-for-supernatural-creatures?p=999632#post999632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hum, maybe... but, what's GLS ? Homo sapiens glutaminase (<i>GLS</i>) is the best result I've found with a google search.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genetic Lycanthropic Syndrome. Which, given the basis on spiritual matters and existence of Fera, is not genetic, not always lycanthropic, and not a syndrome, but that won't stop DNA from thinking otherwise. That change in gravitational anomalies that you can record when they shift shape, hinting at an actual change in mass? We'll find an explanation for it later! Surely, there has to be one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:09:55-08:00","id":999722,"title":"","content":"Trying to depersonalize the concept of &quot;supernatural&quot; in the Technocracy, I did go with &quot;Deviant <b>X</b> #<b>$$$$$$$</b>&quot;<br /> with <b>X</b> a greek letter that define a class of supernatural as the Techno see it,<br /> and <b>$$$$$$$ </b>a 7 numbers digit that identify each individual the Technos would come across<br /> <br /> so, if Joe Longtooth a Cainite Anarch Brujah of XII Generation, die while fighting a Devil-Tiger Keui-jin in some sort of turf war in Los Angeles, and subsequently the Kuei-jin is destroyed by other Anarch allies of Joe,<br /> the Technos will register it as<br /> &lt;&lt;<b>\u03b32486</b> died while fighting <b>\u03b3\u03b1215</b> for hunting territories in Los Angeles, <b>\u03b3\u03b1215</b> has been subsequently destroyed by other pure \u03b3 Deviants allies of <b>\u03b32486</b>&gt;&gt;<br /> because their infos are gained mainly from observation and thus is incomplete (other than they don't really care, if you can kill it with napalm, is fine)<br /> <br /> Note: <b>\u03b32486</b> 's whole name is &quot;<b>Deviant \u03b3</b>[Gamma] <b>#0002486</b>&quot; and <b>\u03b3\u03b1215 </b>is &quot;<b>Deviant \u03b3\u03b1</b> [Gamma-Alpha] <b>#0000215</b>&quot;<br /> as those &quot;strange asian vampires&quot; are registered as a subspecies of vampires, so \u03b3\u03b1 instead than \u03b3<br /> <br /> other classes are<br /> Alpha: Human Willworker, Esper, Witches, Technoshamans<br /> Beta: Teratomorphs (mainly Garou, but other shapeshifter as well)<br /> Gamma: Vampires, Kuei-jin, other types of vampires (chi-mei describes as a whole different subspecies of vampire than Kuei-jin)<br /> Delta: True Mages<br /> Eta: Changelings (pleb kiths)<br /> Theta: Zombies of sorts (sometime even Samedi, if not properly cheked)<br /> Zeta:Fomors<br /> Iota: Other monsters (the occasional Ananasi is registered as Iota Deviant)<br /> Kappa: Non-physical beings (if there's somewhere a written reference about spiritual manifestations, they would be referred as Kappa Deviant rather than fanciful names like &quot;ghosts and spirits&quot; )<br /> Lambda: Changeling Sidhe (they are recent, and the Technos don't have much material on them, therefore for now they are classified as another species)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 11-07-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:39:27-08:00","id":999954,"title":"","content":"The best way would be to replace the subspecies designation for major supernatural creatures or to add an additional subspecies designation for minor supernatural creatures. Garou could be classified as Homo sapiens lupus while Garou Kinfolk would be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens lupus. Kindred could be classified as Homo sapiens sanguis while Ghouls could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens sanguis (Dhampir could be Homo sapiens sapiens cruor while Revenents could be Homo sapiens sapiens caedis). Changelings could be classified as Homo sapiens somnium while Kinain could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens somnium. Kue-jin could be classified as Homo sapiens spiritum while Dhampyr could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens spiritum. Mages could be classified as Homo sapiens magus while Sorcerers could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens magus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:14:52-08:00","id":999970,"title":"","content":"There is a lot of ways to do that, and the Technocracy isn't as uniform as to have only one at use. So I would do something like this:<br /> <br /> Members with a penchant for theorizing about Reality Deviants would probably create their own categorizations based on their personal Paradigm. Some can trade notes at symposiums on the subject, but those categories would vary greatly. Others can simply shove their own categories on their subordinates and work as if it was the norm. An a*****e of those that achieve great status could make some big slices of the Union work under her wordings, but ultimately it is just her way.<br /> <br /> People given to record with precision would probably create some kind of code they see as clear. It will be based on what they deem relevant to highlight. Sometimes it will be good enough to be used by others as a standard. Sometimes it will make sense only to this person. And sometimes, again, she will be powerful enough to force the ones below to follow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T06:53:29-08:00","id":1000250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999628-pseudo-scientific-names-for-supernatural-creatures?p=999954#post999954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way would be to replace the subspecies designation for major supernatural creatures or to add an additional subspecies designation for minor supernatural creatures. Garou could be classified as Homo sapiens lupus while Garou Kinfolk would be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens lupus. Kindred could be classified as Homo sapiens sanguis while Ghouls could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens sanguis (Dhampir could be Homo sapiens sapiens cruor while Revenents could be Homo sapiens sapiens caedis). Changelings could be classified as Homo sapiens somnium while Kinain could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens somnium. Kue-jin could be classified as Homo sapiens spiritum while Dhampyr could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens spiritum. Mages could be classified as Homo sapiens magus while Sorcerers could be classified as Homo sapiens sapiens magus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea, I need to do some research about species' latin name now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:41:47-08:00","id":1000266,"title":"","content":"Well, I would suggest using genus names for the subspecies, as opposed to species names, with the species name added afterwards as an addition subspecies designation afterwards. For example, all human born Garou should generally be Homo sapiens lupus and, if they are related to arctic wolf, should be specifically Homo sapiens lupus arctos (Human Garou Kinfolk would be generally Homo sapiens sapiens lupus and, if they are related to arctic wolves, specifically Homo sapiens sapiens lupus arctos). Of course, there would be an argument over the specific classification of Animal Fera and Animal Kinfolk and Metis Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}